# CASE A variant: the archon approaches a PC who stands still. Put a Chaotic Evil orc barbarian six squares west of a hostile lantern archon,
# then walk him into the archon's Aura of Menace (radius 2) and dump what the
# game says (bd inc-bp44). Read the result with tools/check_aura_of_menace.sh.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/aura-of-menace.keys <seed>
#
# THE STAGING. Wizard mode (src/Player.cpp KY_CMD_WIZMODE) offers "Monster
# Summoning" (src/Debug.cpp case 6). The summoned archon is placed five squares
# east. Freeze Monsters (wizard switch row 10) holds it still, so the walk below
# ends two squares from it every time. Cheat Death (row 0) and Infinite Mana
# (row 7) are set in the same visit, as tools/keys/blind-fight-miss.keys does.
#
# WHY CHAOTIC EVIL. The archon is lawful good and only an evil visitor is hostile
# to it (src/Target.cpp HostilitySmite); a neutral character is "weak neutrality".
# The character is a barbarian because a rogue's Bluff can hide his alignment
# (Creature::isPMType).
#
# THE WALK. Three RIGHT steps leave the barbarian two squares from the archon.
# An orc is light-averse and the archon sheds light, so the game asks "Confirm
# enter the brightly-lit area?"; @while answers it only while it is on screen.

@include aura-of-menace-chargen.keys

SPACE   # dismiss the arrival-room description

# Wizard switches: Cheat Death (row 0), Infinite Mana (row 7). Monsters are NOT
# frozen, so the archon moves.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
DOWN*7
SPACE
ESC

# A hostile ramadeen (a melee charger with no spells, so it closes), six squares east.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "ramadeen"
RIGHT*6 ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:summoned

# The PC waits one turn in place. The ramadeen charges from six squares away
# and strikes once; a second turn could kill a first-level barbarian.
.
@dump:wait1
v
@dump:log
ESC
w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
DOWN*40
@dump:stati
ESC
@quit
